# typesafe-ai

# Build with TypeSafe (Jev) via Vercel AI Gateway

TypeSafe System One models (flagship: **Jev**) return typed decisions and probabilities, not free text. Code owns the workflow; Jev supplies programmable common sense.

**Preferred transport:** Vercel AI Gateway evaluate endpoint (not OpenRouter; evaluation is not on OpenAI-compatible chat endpoints). Direct `api.typesafe.ai` is legacy.

## Before coding
1. Prefer atomic questions: **boolean** (yes/no probability), **choice** (one of N), **score** (ordered rubric). Legacy TypeSafe docs call boolean "noul".
2. Put judgments in `instructions` + `criteria`; put evidence in `state` (string or JSON). Ask independent questions in one request (parallel).
3. Compose answers in code with thresholds; escalate uncertain cases.
4. Gateway docs / model id: `typesafe-ai/jev`. Upstream skill reference: https://github.com/typesafe-ai/skills/tree/main/skills/typesafe-ai

## HTTP (Vercel AI Gateway — preferred)
`POST https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/evaluate` with `Authorization: Bearer $AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`, body:
```json
{
  "model": "typesafe-ai/jev",
  "state": { "...": "..." },
  "questions": {
    "qid": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "instructions": "...",
      "criteria": { "true": "...", "false": "..." }
    }
  }
}
```
Parse `answers.<id>.probability` (0..1). Also accept `VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN` if present.

Override with env `JEV_ENDPOINT` / `JEV_MODEL`. Load keys from process environment or the project’s configured secret store (never log values).

## Legacy HTTP (TypeSafe direct)
`POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone` with `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`, model `jev-latest`, question type `noul`, parse `answers.<id>.noul`. Prefer Gateway when available.

## Contact verification pattern
For directory/scrape quality gates (not full Clay enrichment):
- Deterministic first: syntax, MX, disposable domains, junk name heuristics, dedupe.
- Then Jev batch on survivors / borderline rows with booleans such as:
  - `looks_real_listing` — is this a plausible music-industry contact (venue/radio/blog/playlist/press)?
  - `name_fits_category` — does `name` fit `category`?
  - `contact_plausible` — does email/host look organizationally coherent (not random junk)?
- Keep thresholds in application configuration; sample and validate before a full-scale run.
- Implement a reusable verification gate and pipeline integration; keep deterministic checks separate from model judgments.

## Credentials
Server-side only: `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` (preferred) or `VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN`. Never log keys.

